{"reference":"2 Chronicles 11","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Israel, Judah, and the Temple","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Although the kingdom has divided, this chapter does not treat Judah as the whole story. Its focus is the Davidic king in Judah and worship in Jerusalem, yet it still speaks of priests, Levites, and worshipers who come from across Israel as belonging within “all Israel.” This perspective helps explain why the account gives special attention to their movement to Jerusalem.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 11:13-17"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_011_bea77f8030d4139b2038023e"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}